1|0@SmartThings^1440184876#cub048w:drbudro$:My current system has 3 day battery backup and uses GSM instead of a hardwired internet. It's located centrally in my home with a high gain antenna on my roof to help prevent jamming. If the system misses two pings I'm notified immediately and have the option to have the police alerted. My phone, hard lined internet and power are also monitored. This system was not $3k. There are dozens of home security companies that do this that also have zwave compatibility (but not for under $100). If you're trying to use a consumer home automation system for home security, you're going to be disappointed. I use ST to turn my lights on when I enter a room. I wouldn't trust a $99 device to do anything more than that. Edit: If I bought the v1 hub through the kickstarter I'd probably be disappointed to be honest.
